WEBVTT

00:00:13.150 --> 00:00:15.110
<b><i>BUBUKI/BURANKI</i></b>

00:00:13.280 --> 00:00:15.110
<b>The Gentle Giants of the Galaxy</b>

00:00:29.550 --> 00:00:30.130
BURANKI

00:00:32.460 --> 00:00:33.800
BURANKI

00:00:36.680 --> 00:00:37.590
BURANKI

00:00:56.700 --> 00:00:57.490
Kazuki

00:00:56.700 --> 00:00:57.490
Kaoruko

00:01:26.310 --> 00:01:28.400
<b><i>BUBUKI/BURANKI</i></b>

00:01:27.690 --> 00:01:28.400
<b>The Gentle Giants of the Galaxy</b>

00:01:28.400 --> 00:01:29.940
<b><i>BUBUKI/BURANKI</i></b>

00:01:28.400 --> 00:01:29.940
<b>The Gentle Giants of the Galaxy</b>

00:01:34.960 --> 00:01:37.400
<b>Monday, April 8, 2041</b>

00:01:48.420 --> 00:01:51.300
<i>All operations monopolized by the 
supranational corporation Demokratia</i>

00:01:50.140 --> 00:01:51.300
Time to eat.

00:01:51.300 --> 00:01:54.420
<i>involving humanoid machinery framework</i>

00:01:54.420 --> 00:02:00.430
<i>will be transferred to public corporations 
managed by the APE, per cabinet decision.</i>

00:02:20.360 --> 00:02:20.890
Morning.

00:02:21.370 --> 00:02:22.240
Good morning!

00:02:23.040 --> 00:02:24.110
Morning!

00:02:25.640 --> 00:02:28.750
A-chan, you didn't get your uniform in time?

00:02:29.290 --> 00:02:30.550
Yeah...

00:02:30.550 --> 00:02:32.920
If there's anything else 
you have trouble with,

00:02:32.920 --> 00:02:34.400
ask me anytime.

00:02:35.400 --> 00:02:36.450
Thanks.

00:02:36.450 --> 00:02:38.760
Okay, I gotta run.

00:02:40.770 --> 00:02:42.410
What's up, Kogane?

00:02:42.410 --> 00:02:44.310
You know that new student?

00:02:44.310 --> 00:02:47.200
Oh... Yeah, something like that.

00:02:47.200 --> 00:02:49.720
What do you mean, "something like that"?

00:02:52.080 --> 00:02:53.260
Pardon me.

00:02:54.060 --> 00:02:58.530
<b>Pisces</b>

00:02:54.060 --> 00:02:58.530
<b>Outside Japan</b>

00:02:55.030 --> 00:02:57.290
Kazuki Azuma-kun...

00:02:56.940 --> 00:02:58.530
<b>Acrophobic Tendencies</b>

00:02:57.760 --> 00:02:58.530
I see!

00:02:59.180 --> 00:03:00.530
So you're the...

00:03:02.460 --> 00:03:05.030
Oh, I'm sorry. That was thoughtless of me.

00:03:05.360 --> 00:03:06.800
Please forgive me.

00:03:06.800 --> 00:03:11.290
I can just imagine how much you've 
suffered with "Kazuki" for a surname.

00:03:11.650 --> 00:03:15.970
But you transferring here today 
must be a stroke of fate.

00:03:17.070 --> 00:03:19.840
And we should consider fate a treasure.

00:03:22.250 --> 00:03:23.430
Yes, sir.

00:03:23.900 --> 00:03:27.300
Good answer. Now, I just need 
to confirm a few things...

00:03:27.890 --> 00:03:29.390
<b>Kazuki
Azuma</b>

00:03:29.740 --> 00:03:32.510
Kazuki? The witch's son?

00:03:32.510 --> 00:03:37.200
What? Don't people like that go 
to special schools or something?

00:03:37.200 --> 00:03:39.190
Man, I don't want any trouble.

00:03:39.190 --> 00:03:40.490
Yeah.

00:03:42.730 --> 00:03:44.120
<i>It's been a year.</i>

00:03:44.680 --> 00:03:47.460
<i>My life's become so quiet, 
it's like it isn't even real.</i>

00:03:51.590 --> 00:03:54.400
<i>Hello, Azuma! Long time no see!</i>

00:03:54.400 --> 00:03:57.050
<i>What's up with you? I'm doing good!</i>

00:03:57.430 --> 00:04:00.380
<i>Today, me and four friends 
are going on a journey</i>

00:04:00.840 --> 00:04:04.630
<i>to find out how to bring my 
mother's heart back to life.</i>

00:04:05.190 --> 00:04:08.760
<i>I absolutely will make this happen!</i>

00:04:09.230 --> 00:04:11.900
<i>I'll drop you a line. See you later.</i>

00:04:23.520 --> 00:04:27.070
You've gotta, you know, broaden your view,

00:04:27.070 --> 00:04:29.000
so you can see the whole field.

00:04:29.000 --> 00:04:31.620
You're really addicted now, huh?

00:04:33.370 --> 00:04:34.380
I guess so.

00:04:34.380 --> 00:04:37.630
Well, it's good to have 
something you can get into.

00:04:37.930 --> 00:04:38.640
Yeah.

00:04:44.450 --> 00:04:45.680
By the way,

00:04:45.680 --> 00:04:50.480
I heard Azuma formally 
transferred to a school here in Japan.

00:04:50.480 --> 00:04:51.790
Seems so.

00:04:53.400 --> 00:04:55.190
Have you heard from him?

00:04:56.840 --> 00:05:01.240
I figure he's still too busy, 
since he just transferred.

00:05:01.240 --> 00:05:02.610
True.

00:05:04.170 --> 00:05:08.060
Oh, right! Did you get us 
good seats for Sunday?

00:05:08.060 --> 00:05:11.750
Yeah, you know it! I never fail!

00:05:11.750 --> 00:05:15.070
Thanks! That's my Hiiragi-sama!

00:05:15.070 --> 00:05:17.620
I can always count on you!

00:05:20.210 --> 00:05:21.920
<b>Curry Restaurant</b>

00:05:28.950 --> 00:05:31.430
You there! What are you doing out this late?

00:05:32.840 --> 00:05:34.060
Uh, nothing...

00:05:35.440 --> 00:05:37.160
You don't have to be nervous.

00:05:37.160 --> 00:05:39.060
We're just volunteers.

00:05:39.060 --> 00:05:42.030
Do you have any kind of ID on you?

00:05:43.580 --> 00:05:45.570
No, I don't...

00:05:45.980 --> 00:05:47.910
Are you in high school?

00:05:48.550 --> 00:05:50.320
Yes, I am.

00:05:50.320 --> 00:05:52.370
Then what are you doing—

00:05:52.370 --> 00:05:54.300
It's a dangerous world out there.

00:05:54.740 --> 00:05:57.750
You don't want to get caught 
up in any senseless trouble.

00:05:58.180 --> 00:06:00.060
You'd best head on home.

00:06:01.120 --> 00:06:01.980
Okay.

00:06:02.390 --> 00:06:03.800
Thank you.

00:06:04.180 --> 00:06:06.130
Be careful out there.

00:06:33.260 --> 00:06:34.450
Hey, Kogane.

00:06:34.850 --> 00:06:36.080
Hii-kun!

00:06:38.160 --> 00:06:40.790
Haven't seen you in a while. What's up?

00:06:40.790 --> 00:06:42.410
O-Oh, well...

00:06:42.820 --> 00:06:44.840
Hii-kun, where's Kino-chan?

00:06:44.840 --> 00:06:47.550
I thought I might catch 
her if I waited here.

00:06:47.830 --> 00:06:50.990
She's at practice. You didn't hear?

00:06:50.990 --> 00:06:53.890
She plays lacrosse now.

00:06:54.190 --> 00:06:55.610
Seems out of character, huh?

00:06:55.970 --> 00:06:59.040
But she's taking it pretty seriously.

00:06:59.040 --> 00:07:01.100
Wow, really?

00:07:01.560 --> 00:07:03.490
So what about you?

00:07:04.100 --> 00:07:06.870
Azuma transferred to your school, right?

00:07:07.250 --> 00:07:08.660
You guys getting along good?

00:07:08.660 --> 00:07:11.240
Oh... Yeah, I guess.

00:07:12.250 --> 00:07:14.590
Okay, I'm gonna take off.

00:07:17.150 --> 00:07:19.410
Aren't you going to come visit A-chan?

00:07:21.600 --> 00:07:24.920
Maybe... If I feel like it.

00:07:25.390 --> 00:07:26.550
Oh...

00:07:27.010 --> 00:07:27.990
Besides...

00:07:28.960 --> 00:07:32.260
I'm trying to tell myself 
none of that happened.

00:07:33.240 --> 00:07:36.970
Since that day a year ago, 
when Reoko went into hiding,

00:07:37.330 --> 00:07:40.820
my life has been totally normal.

00:07:41.530 --> 00:07:45.430
I wake up, go to school, then go home.

00:07:45.880 --> 00:07:50.640
If I want to get along with everyone 
around me in that kind of life,

00:07:50.640 --> 00:07:52.990
then I have to be normal, too.

00:07:53.850 --> 00:07:56.760
I have to make like that whole 
journey never happened.

00:07:57.470 --> 00:07:58.990
But...

00:08:08.420 --> 00:08:11.480
So apparently, Laetitia's dad refused

00:08:11.480 --> 00:08:14.970
the government's offer to 
give her a state funeral.

00:08:15.430 --> 00:08:19.910
It was probably out of consideration 
to the other four.

00:08:20.850 --> 00:08:21.660
Mm.

00:08:23.600 --> 00:08:27.480
And? How's high school life going for you?

00:08:27.790 --> 00:08:30.480
Oh... Okay, I guess.

00:08:30.840 --> 00:08:32.070
I see.

00:08:32.590 --> 00:08:34.070
Okay, huh?

00:08:38.020 --> 00:08:42.130
Shuusaku! Could you drive 
a little more carefully?

00:08:42.130 --> 00:08:45.080
Must be careful, please!

00:08:45.080 --> 00:08:47.460
Oh, sure... Sorry.

00:08:49.930 --> 00:08:52.970
Ugh, I'm miserable. It's gotta be twins.

00:08:53.270 --> 00:08:54.230
Really?

00:08:54.230 --> 00:08:57.770
It has to be! I can tell! 
It's woman's intuition!

00:08:57.770 --> 00:08:59.220
By the way,

00:08:59.220 --> 00:09:02.570
I got word from Tsuwabuki this 
morning that he arrived over there.

00:09:05.700 --> 00:09:07.770
Lyudmila, Diana...

00:09:09.050 --> 00:09:11.950
This is truly a beautiful place.

00:09:13.440 --> 00:09:14.590
And...

00:09:15.230 --> 00:09:16.570
What about Reoko?

00:09:18.780 --> 00:09:21.640
I heard from Souya yesterday,

00:09:21.640 --> 00:09:24.430
so I rushed straight over to see her.

00:09:24.850 --> 00:09:30.060
It was her first time waking up in 
the full year since she fell asleep.

00:09:31.160 --> 00:09:35.350
Don't worry. She's not gonna 
die right away or anything.

00:09:35.350 --> 00:09:38.760
You can hear it from Souya at the hospital.

00:09:43.470 --> 00:09:45.730
<b><i>BUBUKI BURANKI</i></b>

00:09:44.640 --> 00:09:45.730
<b>The Gentle Giants of the Galaxy</b>

00:10:03.810 --> 00:10:06.170
What's your problem?! Learn some manners!

00:10:06.170 --> 00:10:08.010
You can't just barge in without knocking!

00:10:08.010 --> 00:10:10.310
There's a lady staying 
in this room, you know!

00:10:10.310 --> 00:10:12.960
I'm calling the doctor! Doctor!

00:10:12.960 --> 00:10:15.260
Doctor! Doctor!

00:10:15.260 --> 00:10:17.130
Sorry! Sorry!

00:10:17.130 --> 00:10:22.450
I didn't explain to him that you're 
well enough to be out of bed now!

00:10:23.730 --> 00:10:25.360
I'm really sorry, Reoko-chan!

00:10:25.360 --> 00:10:26.870
Huh?! What the heck?!

00:10:26.870 --> 00:10:29.920
He came sneaking in here because 
he thought I'd be asleep?!

00:10:29.920 --> 00:10:31.440
That's even worse!

00:10:31.440 --> 00:10:33.940
You creeper! Pervert! Deviant!

00:10:33.940 --> 00:10:37.950
Come on, I said I was sorry! 
Cut me some slack, Reoko-chan!

00:10:38.400 --> 00:10:41.450
I'm begging you! Let us off the hook!

00:10:41.810 --> 00:10:46.700
Besides, didn't I tell you to let me leave 
here as soon as you knew I was healthy?!

00:10:48.420 --> 00:10:51.190
Well, Dr. Arabashiri? You hear me?

00:10:51.190 --> 00:10:52.710
Are you listening?

00:10:53.660 --> 00:10:54.590
Huh?

00:10:54.860 --> 00:10:56.290
Don't "Huh?" me!

00:10:56.290 --> 00:10:59.070
What, you weren't even listening?

00:10:59.070 --> 00:11:00.220
Sorry...

00:11:00.680 --> 00:11:03.470
So how is Reoko doing?

00:11:04.910 --> 00:11:09.480
All her vitals are normal. 
In a word, she's healthy.

00:11:10.020 --> 00:11:15.110
Since that day a year ago, when she lost 
the regenerative ability Entei gave her,

00:11:15.770 --> 00:11:17.900
she's been just a normal person.

00:11:18.330 --> 00:11:22.150
She just regained consciousness, 
so it's too soon to celebrate,

00:11:22.150 --> 00:11:24.790
but thankfully, she doesn't 
show any sign of vagueness.

00:11:25.830 --> 00:11:26.660
It's just...

00:11:27.090 --> 00:11:27.980
Just?

00:11:30.040 --> 00:11:33.900
Reoko-sama has no memories right now.

00:11:33.900 --> 00:11:37.400
Her name, her past, her story...

00:11:37.820 --> 00:11:40.170
Every last memory is gone.

00:11:41.630 --> 00:11:45.990
But you know, Reoko-sama 
was kept alive by Buranki,

00:11:45.990 --> 00:11:48.520
beings that exist outside 
the laws of this world.

00:11:49.040 --> 00:11:53.230
If her memory is all she lost in 
return for being human again,

00:11:53.230 --> 00:11:55.590
maybe it's a small price to pay.

00:11:57.230 --> 00:12:00.690
Well, whether she remembers or not,

00:12:00.690 --> 00:12:05.250
there's no end to the people who 
still hold a grudge against her.

00:12:06.540 --> 00:12:11.750
Besides, this is a special facility that 
was originally built just for Reoko-sama.

00:12:12.220 --> 00:12:16.040
It's got everything, so she'll have 
no difficulty living her life.

00:12:17.090 --> 00:12:20.660
She'll only be missing one thing... freedom.

00:12:21.070 --> 00:12:25.300
Reoko-sama will be a caged bird 
here for the rest of her life.

00:12:25.780 --> 00:12:26.960
But that's...

00:12:28.440 --> 00:12:32.000
Come by again. I'm sure 
it'll make her happy.

00:12:32.840 --> 00:12:35.710
By the way, are Kinoa and 
the other kids doing okay?

00:12:36.630 --> 00:12:37.690
Yeah...

00:12:37.690 --> 00:12:38.990
I think so.

00:12:39.520 --> 00:12:40.350
Good.

00:12:46.890 --> 00:12:47.900
Azuma...

00:12:48.730 --> 00:12:51.930
Live a good, strong life.

00:12:51.930 --> 00:12:54.500
I know that sounds weird coming from me.

00:12:55.740 --> 00:12:56.850
See ya.

00:13:03.340 --> 00:13:06.390
<b>Clover Delivery</b>

00:13:06.850 --> 00:13:09.430
What? What the heck is this?

00:13:09.430 --> 00:13:13.930
Even if you found Mom's stuff,
you didn't have to send it all to me!

00:13:13.930 --> 00:13:16.440
Azuma, you idiot!

00:13:17.960 --> 00:13:20.010
And if you were gonna send a letter,

00:13:20.010 --> 00:13:24.340
send it first and warn me that 
you're about to send the packages!

00:13:24.340 --> 00:13:25.380
Jeez...

00:13:26.710 --> 00:13:31.930
"Kaoruko, did you know? 
Zetsubi-san told me this.

00:13:31.930 --> 00:13:36.540
Apparently, it was Reoko who came 
up with our names way back when."

00:13:36.540 --> 00:13:39.760
What?! Of course I already knew that!

00:13:39.760 --> 00:13:42.710
Reoko told me herself!

00:13:43.120 --> 00:13:48.350
"Migiwa and I came up with 
your names when we were young,

00:13:48.350 --> 00:13:50.490
as the names we wanted to 
give our future children.

00:13:50.490 --> 00:13:54.750
Hmph! To think she kept a 
silly promise we made as children

00:13:54.750 --> 00:13:57.230
and actually used those names for you!"

00:13:57.510 --> 00:13:58.750
What the heck?!

00:13:58.750 --> 00:14:00.880
Just how buddy-buddy were those two?!

00:14:00.880 --> 00:14:03.110
That's so yuri, it's disgusting!

00:14:03.960 --> 00:14:05.490
Kaoruko?

00:14:07.110 --> 00:14:09.050
Ouch...

00:14:11.000 --> 00:14:12.060
What is all this?

00:14:12.060 --> 00:14:14.260
Joan? Are you there?

00:14:14.260 --> 00:14:15.340
Yes...

00:14:15.340 --> 00:14:18.400
Then help me! Please help me!

00:14:18.400 --> 00:14:22.560
I'm stuck and can't move a freaking muscle!

00:14:22.560 --> 00:14:25.190
Uh, b-but... I can't open the door.

00:14:25.900 --> 00:14:29.340
I don't care! Just break 
the damn thing down!

00:14:29.340 --> 00:14:32.760
What?! But if you cause any more problems,

00:14:32.760 --> 00:14:35.210
you'll be evicted!

00:14:32.760 --> 00:14:35.810
<b></b>

00:14:35.210 --> 00:14:39.010
Oh, I know! I'll call the others,
so just sit tight!

00:14:39.010 --> 00:14:40.310
What?!

00:14:40.310 --> 00:14:43.350
Wait! No! No!

00:14:42.820 --> 00:14:45.320
<b>Kaoruko</b>

00:14:43.350 --> 00:14:47.360
Don't leave me here alone!

00:15:46.180 --> 00:15:49.890
Now that you have used the Buranki's 
power to suit your will,

00:15:49.890 --> 00:15:53.500
once this battle is over, you will 
have to return to the human world.

00:15:54.240 --> 00:15:59.910
<i>To the boring life of doing the 
same mundane things day after day.</i>

00:16:00.680 --> 00:16:02.600
<i>When you do that,</i>

00:16:02.600 --> 00:16:06.570
<i>do you think you'll be able 
to consider the life of the</i>

00:16:06.570 --> 00:16:09.440
<i>stinking drunk stumbling 
down the street valuable?!</i>

00:16:09.770 --> 00:16:13.870
<i>Of course you can't! Just like me!</i>

00:16:13.870 --> 00:16:18.240
<i>Your mind has already been
taken over by the Buranki,</i>

00:16:18.240 --> 00:16:19.990
<i>Kazuki Azuma!</i>

00:16:41.930 --> 00:16:45.400
And then, and then... I was really...

00:16:45.830 --> 00:16:48.220
What, Kogane? What's wrong?

00:16:48.820 --> 00:16:52.030
Oh, nothing, nothing.

00:17:23.500 --> 00:17:24.730
Welcome back,

00:17:25.790 --> 00:17:27.770
children of Migiwa.

00:17:27.770 --> 00:17:30.400
This is what it means to protect a country.

00:17:30.400 --> 00:17:32.950
I'll destroy Entei and end my own life.

00:17:32.950 --> 00:17:33.990
I believe I could die.

00:17:33.990 --> 00:17:37.280
Perhaps I really have only seen 
humans for all this time.

00:17:37.280 --> 00:17:39.910
Let's go together, Azuma!

00:17:55.820 --> 00:17:56.800
A-chan...

00:17:57.560 --> 00:17:58.930
Kogane-chan.

00:17:59.770 --> 00:18:05.140
Even after we went on such an epic journey 
and had adventures together,

00:18:05.730 --> 00:18:10.870
we never see or talk to the others anymore.

00:18:11.400 --> 00:18:12.220
Yeah.

00:18:13.150 --> 00:18:17.670
But I can't just pretend 
none of that ever happened.

00:18:18.190 --> 00:18:21.990
I mean, the five of us 
going to Treasure Island

00:18:21.990 --> 00:18:23.950
and traveling the world together...

00:18:24.460 --> 00:18:28.180
To me... To me, they're...

00:18:30.150 --> 00:18:33.960
I swear, you're so awkward, Kogane.

00:18:35.340 --> 00:18:36.340
Kino-chan!

00:18:36.770 --> 00:18:39.880
Jeez, what's there to cry about?

00:18:39.880 --> 00:18:44.500
There's no reason to pretend 
our journey never happened.

00:18:44.500 --> 00:18:48.850
We can just keep it safely locked 
up in our hearts. Right?

00:18:49.430 --> 00:18:52.260
Kino-chan... Yeah!

00:18:53.440 --> 00:18:54.190
Here.

00:18:54.820 --> 00:18:56.300
Thanks.

00:19:00.480 --> 00:19:02.630
We're the only ones who know

00:19:03.400 --> 00:19:06.700
what the other four keep 
tucked away in their hearts.

00:19:06.700 --> 00:19:07.910
Shizuru!

00:19:07.910 --> 00:19:09.230
Shizuru-chan!

00:19:10.960 --> 00:19:14.550
Shizuru-chan, Shizuru-chan! I've missed you!

00:19:14.550 --> 00:19:15.140
Yeah.

00:19:15.140 --> 00:19:17.660
Hey, Shizuru! It's been ages!

00:19:17.660 --> 00:19:18.550
Yeah.

00:19:20.100 --> 00:19:23.300
What the heck? So we all ended up here?

00:19:23.300 --> 00:19:24.930
Hiiragi!

00:19:24.130 --> 00:19:24.930
Hiiragi.

00:19:24.930 --> 00:19:26.680
Hii-kun! Why are you here?

00:19:27.960 --> 00:19:31.690
Kogane, I'm telling myself 
that journey never happened.

00:19:33.740 --> 00:19:35.010
But you know...

00:19:36.060 --> 00:19:40.950
There's nothing wrong with remembering 
it just once a year, right?

00:19:40.950 --> 00:19:43.870
Hii-kun! Yeah, yeah, yeah, yeah!

00:19:43.870 --> 00:19:46.070
Jeez, you're so difficult.

00:19:47.660 --> 00:19:49.370
Are you two dating?

00:19:50.110 --> 00:19:51.870
You ask that <i>now</i>?!

00:19:54.380 --> 00:19:56.150
Oh, bull's eye.

00:19:56.150 --> 00:19:57.000
We're not!

00:19:57.000 --> 00:19:59.170
Oh, you're in perfect harmony.

00:19:59.170 --> 00:20:00.510
We are not!

00:20:02.480 --> 00:20:06.550
Hey, so our great heart finally shows up.

00:20:06.550 --> 00:20:07.770
A-chan!

00:20:08.430 --> 00:20:11.850
I'm not your heart anymore.

00:20:14.180 --> 00:20:16.070
Since that battle ended,

00:20:16.690 --> 00:20:18.950
my heart won't even move.

00:20:19.550 --> 00:20:22.310
It might never do anything again.

00:20:23.230 --> 00:20:24.740
A-chan...

00:20:30.200 --> 00:20:31.610
Mine now!

00:20:32.160 --> 00:20:36.010
Huh... I guess hearts are 
lighter than I thought.

00:20:36.010 --> 00:20:39.730
It always stops right when 
you need it to work, though.

00:20:39.730 --> 00:20:42.210
What a piece of junk.

00:20:42.720 --> 00:20:43.550
I'm sure...

00:20:44.620 --> 00:20:49.610
I'm sure it stops when pain 
fills A-chan's heart.

00:20:50.010 --> 00:20:53.140
Right. Oubu is protecting Azuma,

00:20:53.810 --> 00:20:59.370
so that its precious heart won't have 
to fight any battles while feeling sad.

00:21:01.210 --> 00:21:03.280
Well, that makes things simple, then!

00:21:04.480 --> 00:21:07.090
We can't share physical pain.

00:21:07.550 --> 00:21:12.300
But if you're talking emotional pain, 
we can understand that a little, right?

00:21:14.600 --> 00:21:18.010
Azuma, seriously, thanks for everything!

00:21:18.010 --> 00:21:18.840
Thanks!

00:21:18.840 --> 00:21:22.740
H-Huh? I feel like this 
is wrong somehow, but...

00:21:22.740 --> 00:21:24.010
Thanks.

00:21:26.380 --> 00:21:29.510
Wait... What do you mean by that?

00:21:30.260 --> 00:21:33.100
You're totally making fun of me, aren't you?!

00:21:33.100 --> 00:21:35.140
Kinoa! Hiiragi!

00:21:35.140 --> 00:21:37.940
Whoa! Azuma's mad!

00:21:39.370 --> 00:21:42.060
Give me back the heart, Hiiragi!

00:21:42.060 --> 00:21:43.590
For crying out loud!

00:21:44.140 --> 00:21:47.390
You look kinda cool when 
you're mad, A-zu-ma.

00:21:47.390 --> 00:21:49.690
What did you say?!

00:21:51.010 --> 00:21:54.140
Since we're all together, 
let's go somewhere.

00:21:54.140 --> 00:21:55.050
Where?

00:21:55.050 --> 00:21:56.640
I know! Treasure Island!

00:21:56.640 --> 00:21:58.120
That doesn't exist anymore!

00:22:01.170 --> 00:22:04.340
Let's go find the next new Treasure Island.

00:22:04.340 --> 00:22:06.050
Great idea!

00:22:08.830 --> 00:22:10.040
There we go!

00:22:10.040 --> 00:22:11.330
Zoom!

00:22:11.330 --> 00:22:13.000
O-ho-ho-ho.

00:22:14.200 --> 00:22:15.440
Yahoo!

00:22:14.840 --> 00:22:15.860
Yeah!

00:22:15.860 --> 00:22:19.080
What a lovely view. What a lovely view.

00:23:11.640 --> 00:23:13.460
Hey, A-chan!

00:23:13.460 --> 00:23:15.830
Which way should we go?

00:23:18.200 --> 00:23:19.580
Keep going straight!

00:23:19.920 --> 00:23:21.460
Straight ahead!

00:23:21.710 --> 00:23:22.850
Okay!

00:23:22.850 --> 00:23:23.620
Roger.

00:23:23.620 --> 00:23:24.590
Got it!

00:23:24.590 --> 00:23:25.970
You can count on us!

00:23:35.850 --> 00:23:40.620
<b>Episode 24</b>

00:23:35.850 --> 00:23:40.620
<b>The Adventurers</b>
